hp-check[19916]: info: :Note: hp-check can be run in three modes:
hp-check[19916]: info: :1. Compile-time check mode (-c or --compile): Use this mode     
hp-check[19916]: info: :before compiling the HPLIP supplied tarball (.tar.gz or .run) to
hp-check[19916]: info: :determine if the proper dependencies are installed to           
hp-check[19916]: info: :successfully compile HPLIP.                                     
hp-check[19916]: info: :2. Run-time check mode (-r or --run): Use this mode to determine
hp-check[19916]: info: :if a distro supplied package (.deb, .rpm, etc) or an already    
hp-check[19916]: info: :built HPLIP supplied tarball has the proper dependencies        
hp-check[19916]: info: :installed to successfully run.                                  
hp-check[19916]: info: :3. Both compile- and run-time check mode (-b or --both)         
hp-check[19916]: info: :(Default): This mode will check both of the above cases (both   
hp-check[19916]: info: :compile- and run-time dependencies).                            
